      "id": 1,
      "text": "Carbon Cliff earned its name from the many coal mines that dotted the bluff west of town in the mid‑19th century.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Cliff%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Chicago and Rock Island railroad reached Carbon Cliff in 1854, sparking the village’s early growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Cliff%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The bluffs also yielded rich clay, leading to the 1865 founding of Argillo Works, a leading fire‑brick producer.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16,
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Cliff%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the early 20th century, coal supplies were nearly exhausted, ending mining operations in the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        13,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Cliff%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1906, residents petitioned the county court to incorporate as a village, formalizing Carbon Cliff’s municipal status.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carbon_Cliff%2C_Illinois",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
